[Annotator "https://lichess.org/@/RyanFourLC"]
[FEN "rqb2rk1/pp1pppbp/2p1nnp1/8/2P1N3/1P3N2/PB1PPPPP/RQ2KB1R w KQ - 2 7"]
[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2021.10.24"]
[UTCTime "17:44:47"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

7. Bxf6 exf6 (7... Bxf6) 8. Qb2 { Opponent has given up their best counter to our dark squared bishop, if we can defend the f6 pawn we will be comfortable. } 8... Qf4 9. d3 { If we can get rid of the e4 knight we are completely safe, try to force it away. } 9... d5 (9... f5 { This allows Nf6+, which is incredibly annoying. }) (9... Ng5 { This move is probably fine, but try to get rid of the enemy knight more forcefully. }) 10. e3 { This is the only difficult move to deal with that remains. Consider it a puzzle, if you just want to know the move, press the get hint button. } 10... dxe4!! { A queen sacrifice for two knights, the reason this is good will become apparent very soon. } (10... Qg4 { This undefends our f6 pawn. }) (10... Qh6 { This undefends our f6 pawn. }) (10... Qf5 { This move gets the queen trapped!
Ng3 Qg4 h3 and the queen is lost. } 11. Ng3 Qg4 12. h3) 11. exf4 exf3 { Now the e-file is wide open, and all we have to do is put a bishop somewhere on that file to get checkmate. } 12. O-O-O { The only hope for opponent is to try to put a rook on the e-file to trade away the bishop that will deliver check. But, now the enemy king is very vulnerable to our dark squared bishop. } 12... f5 13. d4 { The only move that doesn't hang mate, and saves the queen. Remember that now we can checkmate the opponent by getting a bishop onto the e-file. } 13... Nxd4 (13... Nc5 { There is a better knight move. }) (13... Nc7 { There is a better knight move. }) (13... Nd8 { There is a better knight move. }) (13... Nxf4 { There is a better knight move. }) (13... Ng5 { There is a better knight move. }) 14. Re1 { Again the only move that doesn't hang mate. Now find the tactical finisher. } 14... Ne2+ 15. Rxe2 { Now both of Bxb2 and xe2 will win. We will look at Bxb2. } 15... Bxb2+ 16. Rxb2 { Note that Be6 is one turn too late to be checkmate. } 16... Bd7 { Be8 will be checkmate, just in time. Opponent must sacrifice the rook to stop it. } 17. Re2 fxe2 *


