12. f5 { This is another attempt at defending this position for white, and there are probably several paths to victory, but try to find a knight move that attacks several weak squares in the enemy position. } 12... Nf4 { Opponent now definitely has to castle to try to control the e-file and keep the bishops away. } 13. O-O-O { There is only one thing currently preventing Be6#. } 13... Bxf5 (13... gxf5 { quadrupled pawns is of course very good, but there is a slightly better way of capturing the f5 pawn }) 14. Re1 { There are again probably several ways to win, but take advantage of the fact that the white bishop needs to remain defending d3, otherwise a game-ending fork will occur. } 14... fxg2 { Now there is no way for opponent to retain the only queen. We can stop here as it is very clearly game over. } *


