1. b4 { 1. b4 is barely different from 1. c4 at all. } 1... Nf6 2. Nf3 Ne6 3. Bb2 g6 4. Nc3 { If opponent moved the c-pawn here, we'd just transpose to an almost identical version of 1.c4. But doing this knight move is completely unimpressive, as it can't move to either of d5/e4. } 4... Bg7 { Here opponent has nothing, so 1. b4 will either transpose to 1.c4 or allow you to reach the setup with no difficulty. } *


